{
 "note": "Margaret River Hotel, 125 Bussell Hwy on the Willmott Ave corner (State Register 2008), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), 2019 street photos and the inHerit record. The 1936 two-storey Inter-War Old English hotel (architect F G B Hawkins, built by C Arnott): taupe rendered brick, Marseille-pattern terracotta tiles, three street gables with white barges and white battens on brown, a long gabled main range with a north gable to Willmott Ave, a tall rendered chimney, the single-storey gabled entry porch on white posts with the hotel sign, and the 1985 single-storey wing behind the south end (outbuilding, so it doesn't move the centre). The rear yard (old motel units and beer garden) was a building site in the 2026 aerial (Heytesbury redevelopment), so only the 1936 building and its south wing are here. Name in plain lettering, no logo. Metres: x left to right as seen from Bussell Hwy (north to south), y back (east) from the front of the south wing.",
